    },
    {
     "kind": "read",
     "step": "read",
     "title": "From secant to tangent",
     "paras": [
      "P is (a, f(a)) and Q is (a + h, f(a + h)).",
      "Slope of PQ: (f(a + h) − f(a))/h.",
      "As h gets closer to 0, Q moves to P and PQ becomes the tangent."
     ],
     "note": "Slope of the tangent = instantaneous rate of change.",
     "ref": "Definition 2.5",
     "id": "g12.maths.u2.s2-1-3.2"
    },
    {
     "kind": "read",
     "step": "read",
     "title": "Procedure",
     "paras": [
